    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="IRS990ScheduleO" softwareId="24020490" softwareVersionNum="2024v5.2">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>A DRAFT OF THE FORM 990 IS SENT TO THE FINANCE COMMITTEE FOR REVIEW PRIOR TO FILING. THE FIVE MEMBER EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE COMPLETES AN IN-DEPTH REVIEW PRIOR TO FILING.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>WHEN INDIVIDUALS JOIN THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS THEY ARE REQUIRED TO REVIEW AND SIGN USRF'S CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY. BOARD MEMBERS ARE RESPONSIBLE FOR DISCLOSING ANY ACTUAL OR POTENTIAL CONFLICTS OF INTEREST AT THE TIME OF SIGNING, AS WELL AS IF/WHEN ONE ARISES AFTER THEY HAVE JOINED THE BOARD. AFTER JOINING THE BOARD CONFLICTS OF INTEREST ARE REPORTED TO THE EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE EVALUATES THE COMPENSATION OF THE EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR ON AN ANNUAL BASIS IN RELATION TO HIS PERFORMANCE AS WELL AS COMPARATIVE DATA FOR SIMILARLY SIZED NATIONAL ORGANIZATIONS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
